Rewritten: the repository's integrations/agent-plugin, two prose skills for a
host agent -- sem-code-review and weave-merge-preview -- became one Nodecode
tool cell. Where the skills told a model to type shell commands at Sem and Weave
and prefix each one with SEM_NO_NETWORK=1 SEM_NO_TELEMETRY=1, the cell builds
the arguments of `sem find', `sem diff', `sem impact' and `weave preview'
itself, lays that prefix on every call (offline is a setting), runs the CLIs in
the asking session's repository through nlk:run-bounded, and hands back what
they printed. Their prose survives: the smallest-query advice, the caveats
that static callers and tests can be incomplete, that a clean merge preview is
not verification, and that nothing here edits, stages, commits or merges are
the tools' descriptions and the (help :sem) topic. Left out: `sem check'
(which runs a repository's own build, linter and tests), and Weave's setup and
land verbs -- the plugin's skills were preview-only and said so; also the
plugin's Python smoke test, whose two cases are now Lisp tests with every CLI
call stubbed. The CLIs themselves are not bundled: the user installs Sem and,
optionally, Weave, exactly as before.
